; Path commands of the crusaders: 6 handler addresses
;
; Indexed by the command byte of a path script pair (#R$B218): #R$B1F3 reads word n and writes it over the handler word
; of the slot, so the crusader runs that handler from the next frame on.
; .
; 0 #R$B1D4 keep running (the handler itself: nothing changes)
; 1 #R$B163 step up 8 pixels (x speed $00A0, curve #R$B0E8)
; 2 #R$B10C hop in place over a pit (x speed $0150, curve #R$B100)
; 3 #R$B139 fall 16 pixels (x speed unchanged, curve #R$B0F4)
; 4 #R$B08E remove the crusader (free the slot)
; 5 #R$B1CF signal the end of the cutscene, then keep running
@label=PathCommands
w$B20C DEFW $B1D4 ; 0: UpdateCrusader, keep running
 $B20E DEFW $B163 ; 1: UpdateCrusaderStepUp
 $B210 DEFW $B10C ; 2: UpdateCrusaderHop
 $B212 DEFW $B139 ; 3: UpdateCrusaderFall
 $B214 DEFW $B08E ; 4: FreeEntitySlotAtEntry
 $B216 DEFW $B1CF ; 5: UpdateCrusaderSignal
